"Let $\\mathcal{C}_n$ be the cone constrained by the Laplacian minor of a leafed $n$-cycle, and let $\\lambda=(\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{n-1})$ be an integer point of $\\mathcal{C}_n$. For a non-negative integer $m$, consider the integer points with first coordinate $\\lambda_0=m$.\n\n**Cyclically distinct composition conjecture.** The number of integer points $\\lambda\\in\\mathcal{C}_n$ with $\\lambda_0=m$ is equal to the number of compositions of $m$ into $n$ parts that are cyclically distinct.\n\nThis conjecture would provide a combinatorial interpretation for the coefficients of $\\sigma_{\\mathcal{C}_n}(q)$."